From fe5096e13cb00e94e8aaef7d1878bac5e7278d41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen De Vleeschauwer <kdv@kdvelectronics.eu>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:17:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mtb: Add Micro Trace Buffer support and the mon mtb command

Backport of MTB support from blackmagic-rtthread (ac9c16ff, cortexm
command registration from f8a58382) to the firmware.

The CoreSight component scan now records the base address of a Micro
Trace Buffer (MTB-M0+, Cortex-M23/M33 MTB, STAR-MC1 MTB) instead of
skipping it, and `mon mtb [status|dump|size]` shows the MTB state, dumps
the recorded branch trace, or sizes the trace buffer.

Firmware specific changes:
- Built unconditionally, like mon dwt: the component scan always calls
  cortexm_mtb_probe(), so the fork's ENABLE_MTB switch is dropped.
- cortexm_mtb_probe() lives in cortexm.c as in the fork.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
